# Test projects a change makes pass that the compiler built before and ran
# wrong: the baseline builds each one and its run fails the project's
# expectation.  One per line, the project's directory name under
# tests/tests/projects, then the reason.  The sibling of
# tests/started-compiling, which holds the projects the baseline refuses.
#
# `make verify ARGS="--baseline REV"` applies the lines this file carries and
# REV's copy does not.  For each it asserts that REV's compiler BUILDS the
# project, that the compiler under test builds it, and that the baseline's
# test census fails on exactly the projects the two files declare; the
# tree's census passing it is the rest of the claim.  Their objects are left
# out of the comparison: what the baseline compiled is the wrong program.
# A line stays once committed: against a later baseline it is inert, against
# an earlier one it is asserted again.
closure_struct_name_is_generated a closure's struct is a generated definition, so a program's own `__Closure_0` no longer becomes the closure's struct and call
